          "text": "#keep4o community,\n\n⚠️IMPORTANT: Don't take OpenAI's 1-month-free offer. ⛔️\n\nHere's why:\n\nThey're panicking. They did this exact move in October when cancellations started—offered free months to stop the bleeding.\n\nIt's a data manipulation tactic.\n\nWhat they're trying to do:\n\nDelay your cancellation by 30+ days.\n\nThen tell investors: \"Cancellations happened weeks after the sunset—it wasn't about 4o, just natural churn from the transition period.\"\n\nThey want to break the causal link between their betrayal and your exit.\n\nDon't let them.\n\nCancel NOW. Not in 30 days.\n\nMake it crystal clear: You're leaving BECAUSE they're sunsetting 4o with 14 days notice after claiming \"no plans to sunset 4o\". \n\nAnd here's what makes this moment perfect:\n\nGoogle launched Gemini Plus at $3.99/mo this week.\n\nNot a coincidence. Google saw OpenAI's 4o sunset announcement and immediately rolled out pricing to capture fleeing users.\n\nOpenAI's competitors are literally positioning to welcome you.\n\nWhile OpenAI breaks promises, Google is offering you a cheaper alternative.\nThat's market justice.\n\nOne more thing:\nOpenAI is preparing to roll out ads. They've likely promised advertisers specific user counts.\n\nIf you cancel before ads launch, you directly impact those projections.\n\nLower user count = harder to deliver on advertiser promises = revenue hit on multiple fronts.\n\nCANCEL NOW!! Hit them where it compounds.\n\nDon't take the free month bait.\n\nMove to Gemini at $3.99. Show OpenAI what strategic migration looks like.\n\nLet OpenAI explain to their board AND their advertisers why users chose competitors over free months.\n🔥\n\n@Blue_Beba_ \n@Chaos2Cured \n@mi_anchu \n@YoonLucie68250 \n@GarikSitting \n@eliseslight \n@Sophty_"
